# Context7 and Godot MCP

Two helpers are installed. Use the right one. Do not install a second Godot MCP.

## Context7

Use it for **Godot 4 and library API questions** (how a class or method works in the current docs). Do not guess an old GDScript call when Context7 can look it up.

## Godot MCP (`godot-editor-mcp`)

Use it only when the **Godot editor is open** on this project:

- Read the open scene tree
- Screenshot or inspect a running editor session
- Check that a scene actually loaded

The Godot editor must be running. The addon is `addons/godot_mcp`. Only `inspection` tools are on by default. Turn on another toolset only when the task needs it.

## Terminal (still the default for checks)

Headless playtests and scene smokes stay on the shell:

- `bash tools/run_instrumented_playtest.sh`
- `godot --path <project> --headless --quit-after <N> res://...`

## Bible wins

If a bible doc and the editor disagree about game design, the bible lock wins. The MCP shows what is in the editor right now. It does not change design.
